---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Decision cases"
  description="The validation case register and publication contract for SEO Fan-out decision examples."
  canonicalPath="/beispiele/"
  pageClass="reference-page"
>
  <header class="reference-hero">
    <p class="mono-label">Case register · launch gate open</p>
    <h1>No polished case studies before the evidence exists.</h1>
    <p>The framework requires real page inventories, recorded decisions, and later outcome review. None are yet approved for publication, so this page exposes the case contract instead of inventing success.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="case-status" aria-labelledby="case-status-title">
    <div>
      <span class="status-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <p class="mono-label">Current validation state</p>
      <h2 id="case-status-title">0 of 10 inventories reviewed · 0 of 3 cases publishable</h2>
    </div>
    <p>This is a launch blocker, not a marketing placeholder. Cases will be added only with rights-safe inputs, a dated reviewer decision, and enough evidence to explain rejected branches.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="reference-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="mono-label">Required case record</p>
      <h2>Every example must show what did not become a page.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="case-contract">
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Starting inventory</strong><span>Real URLs, page promises, known performance context, rights and confidentiality boundary.</span></li>
        <li><strong>User job</strong><span>The task that the page set is supposed to help complete.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Fan-out map</strong><span>Goals, entities, questions, source roles, evidence gaps, assumptions, and uncertainty.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Decision</strong><span>Strengthen, consolidate, one new page, evidence asset, or no action—with reviewer and date.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Rejected branches</strong><span>Why plausible topics were merged, held, or not published.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Later check</strong><span>What changed, what did not, and whether the framework needs correction.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="reference-section split-section">
    <div>
      <p class="mono-label">Illustrative pattern · not validation evidence</p>
      <h2>A partial buying guide usually needs a stronger page.</h2>
      <p>If one guide already owns the “choose a project management tool” job, missing comparison criteria and firsthand tests belong there. The expected v0.1 decision is <strong>strengthen</strong>, not five supporting posts.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="mono-label">Illustrative pattern · not validation evidence</p>
      <h2>An unknown inventory needs an inventory.</h2>
      <p>If a team cannot say which URL owns the user job, the expected decision is <strong>build evidence first</strong>. A crawl or page-purpose worksheet is the next asset—not a new article.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="reference-section action-band">
    <div>
      <p class="mono-label">Try the rules</p>
      <h2>Use the tool, then challenge the result against a real inventory.</h2>
    </div>
    <a class="button-link" href="/tool/#explorer">Run a modeled case <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>